@@ -303,7 +303,22 @@ vpsfree-kb-verify --root "$ROOT" --config-a "$CONFIG_A" --config-b "$CONFIG_B" \
 ```
 
 The predecessor's runtime and source metadata come from the same immutable
-reference. Later phases require matching completed campaign receipts. An
+reference, fixed to
+`github:vpsfreecz/vpsfree-kb-contracts/7dc4d70830e535f4559bccfa668cf65cdce1de2d`.
+This experiment verifies that exact K-runtime upgrade and live artifact/import/
+closure continuity. Both versions use the same vpsAdmin pin; it does not verify
+a vpsAdmin upgrade or compatibility with other predecessor revisions.
+
+The predecessor performs one SSH host-key scan per endpoint and has no readiness
+retry. Its runner also inherits its parent's POSIX session and can leave its
+control socket after shutdown. Run this finite experiment in a durable ordinary
+host service that retains descendants after the controller exits. Use the final
+public controller for stop and update, with its live authenticated shutdown
+handoff. A failed start cannot be resumed as an accepted artifact. Preserve a
+native failure and stop the experiment; do not patch the predecessor, replay the
+failed campaign or substitute host-key trust.
+
+Later phases require matching completed campaign receipts. An
 incomplete phase retains its stage evidence and owned state; it cannot silently
 become another campaign or authorize cleanup.
 Failed public commands retain their native exit and diagnostic output privately
@@ -331,6 +346,26 @@ The continuity phase starts A from the final package and B from the predecessor.
 It uses the final public controller to stop the predecessor runner, resumes B
 with the genuine predecessor package, then updates B through the final public
 command. This does not certify the predecessor's own stop implementation.
+Both historical shutdown crossings require explicit service preparation through
+the genuine predecessor's public SSH command. In the same guarded remote script,
+the verifier checks the attested guest identity digest and current system
+closure, then stops only `vpsadmin-console-router.service`. It requires the
+loaded unit to be inactive/dead, with `MainPID=0` and `Result=success`. RabbitMQ,
+SSH and the guest store remain running. Preparation occurs before the first
+final-controller stop and again after genuine predecessor resume, before update.
+
+Each preparation has a 360-second guest command budget and a separate
+360-second caller observation budget, including transport. Native command
+failure and caller expiry remain distinct. Expiry does not prove cancellation
+of a remote job. Any failed preparation ends the finite campaign; stop or
+update must not follow it. Final boot must restore the normally enabled router
+before capture. The final runner's ordinary stop is also verified without this
+historical preparation.
+
+The resulting upgrade claim includes this explicit guest-service preparation.
+It does not certify ordinary unprepared historical shutdown. The predecessor's
+first SSH scan and service drain may still fail; preserve that failure rather
+than repeat the campaign for a different timing outcome.
 All six credential files, disk identities and
 root/data sentinels must survive; run/artifact identities and actual guest system
 closures must change as specified by update. A remains healthy during that work.
